WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.360
Two voices.

2
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:05.620
One flows like music,
in long golden lines.

3
00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.440
The other is jagged and rough.

4
00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:13.390
In Act 3, Iago talks in animals:
"Were they as prime as goats,

5
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:17.510
as hot as monkeys," In
Act 4, Othello cries out,

6
00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.380
"Goats and monkeys!"

7
00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:21.550
Those animals were never his.

8
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.350
So how did Iago get into his words?

9
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.050
In this mission, you'll set
the two voices side by side:

10
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:32.650
Othello's grand verse, and
Iago's coarse prose and images.

11
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:36.550
You'll read what Othello says
just before he collapses in Act 4,

12
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.960
and ask what has happened to his verse.

13
00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:41.890
And you'll hunt for other lines
Othello may have picked up,

14
00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.760
and ask where they came from.

15
00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:48.060
Your mission: explain how
Iago got into Othello's words.
